# review. `require_code_owner_reviews` stays `false` (`AC-REQCHECK-2`, unchanged) — so
# these rows still do not by themselves REQUIRE a code-owner review and cannot block a
# merge on that basis alone. Becomes blocking via review only if the owner separately
# enables code-owner review, an owner-side decision no agent makes (OQ-2). Original
# clause, retained verbatim: "`required_status_checks` is absent and
# `require_code_owner_reviews` is `false` on this repo's branch protection (verified
# live) — these rows ROUTE review to the owner and make an unreviewed change visible;
# they do not REQUIRE review and cannot block a merge."
